    src: https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Alt%C4%B1kula%C3%A7_Sarcophagus_Combat_scene_%28detail%29.jpg/250px-Alt%C4%B1kula%C3%A7_Sarcophagus_Combat_scene_%28detail%29.jpg
    width: 4182
    height: 2647
    caption: "Armoured cavalry: Achaemenid Dynast of Hellespontine Phrygia
      attacking a Greek psiloi, Altıkulaç Sarcophagus, early 4th century BC."
  - file: BeachedShipsMarathon.jpg
    src: https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/BeachedShipsMarathon.jpg/250px-BeachedShipsMarathon.jpg
    width: 600
    height: 351
    caption: Reconstitution of Persian landing ships at the Battle of Marathon.
  - file: Ship_dashed_against_ship,_till_the_Persian_Army_dead_strewed_the_deep_like_flowers.jpg
    src: https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Ship_dashed_against_ship%2C_till_the_Persian_Army_dead_strewed_the_deep_like_flowers.jpg/250px-Ship_dashed_against_ship%2C_till_the_Persian_Army_dead_strewed_the_deep_like_flowers.jpg
    width: 1750
    height: 2453
    caption: Greek ships against Achaemenid ships at the Battle of Salamis.
  - file: BehistunInscriptiondetail.jpg
    src: https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/BehistunInscriptiondetail.jpg/250px-BehistunInscriptiondetail.jpg
    width: 1280
    height: 841
    caption: A section of the Old Persian part of the trilingual Behistun
      inscription. Other versions are in Babylonian and Elamite.
  - file: Aramaic_translation_of_the_behistun_inscripton.png
    src: https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Aramaic_translation_of_the_behistun_inscripton.png/250px-Aramaic_translation_of_the_behistun_inscripton.png
    width: 700
    height: 705
    caption: The Behistun papyrus, a copy of the Behistun inscription in Aramaic
