    One sentence in "Languages" is corrupt in the source: "It is then likely
    that although Elamite was used by the capital government in Susa, it was
    not a standardized language of g" followed by a broken citation-needed
    template. Since there is no way to know what it claimed, the sentence is
    dropped rather than completed.


    Images that appear in the article body but are not named in the front
