      <td>[[ King of Persia | list-of-kings-of-persia ]]. Ruling for 47 years, Artaxerxes II was the longest reigning Achaemenid king. His birth name was Arses.

      <td>405–358 BC

    <tr
      <td>!![[ Artaxerxes III ]]!!

      <td>[[ King of Persia | list-of-kings-of-persia ]] in addition to [[ Pharaoh of Egypt | list-of-pharaohs ]], having re-conquered the land after it was lost during the reign of Artaxerxes II. His birth name was Ochus.

      <td>358–338 BC

    <tr
      <td>!![[ Artaxerxes IV ]]!!

      <td>[[ King of Persia | list-of-kings-of-persia ]] in addition to [[ Pharaoh of Egypt | list-of-pharaohs ]]. His birth name was Arses.

      <td>338–336 BC

    <tr
      <td>!![[ Darius III ]]!!

      <td>[[ King of Persia | list-of-kings-of-persia ]] in addition to [[ Pharaoh of Egypt | list-of-pharaohs ]]; last ruler of the empire. His birth name was either Artashata or Codomannus.

      <td>336–330 BC

[[ ^d ]]: Also called the !!Achaemenian Empire!!, the !!Persian Empire!!, !!Ancient Persia!!, !!Old Persia!!, or the !!First Persian Empire!!.

